:: StoryTitle
Cloakroom

:: StoryData
{
  "ifid": "<generated by Twine>",
  "format": "Inkjot",
  "format-version": "0.6.0",
  "start": "eight"
}

:: Inklink [config]
(((
Ex 6, the public cut: one evening, three names, and the machinery of the
full Ex 6 (which lives in the Inklinks Library), in a story of its own. A
draft for Inkjot v0.6; `inkjot check` refuses much of it until v0.6 is
built.

New Year's Eve, 1961, at the Hotel Bellevue on the lake at Seeberg. You
keep the cloakroom: a hundred coats, a hundred tickets, and nothing in
any pocket that is your business. A telegram for a guest who doesn't
exist comes to you to hold, wet from the snow. Someone in the hotel is
selling something at midnight, under three names.

Two notebooks race. Yours: what you decide is true, checked for notes
that can't both hold. His: what the doorman and the cigarette girl tell
him, and what he reads in yours. You can feed his lies.

The truth, for the Inker (spoilers):

| Name | Who |
|---|---|
| WREN | Anton Keller, the assistant manager: the seller |
| Mr. Lark | Anton Keller: the name on room 9 |
| the Organist | Vera Duclos, who sings with the band: the signal at midnight |

Felix Orme, the third suspect, is what he says he is: a journalist.
)))
kind: story-game
tags: noir ~ espionage ~ deduction ~ new year
ages: 14..
mode: solo
pov: attendant
start: cloakroom
default moves: walk
default cost: time

(((
Time. One turn is one chronon. The hours are uneven (nine, ten and eleven
take two turns each); the evening is one round of hours: eight turns from
eight o'clock to midnight. Four quarter-hours to spend each turn.
)))
period hour: eight 1, nine 2, ten 2, eleven 2, midnight 1
period evening: new_years_eve ~ of hour
clock: new_years_eve.eight ..= new_years_eve.midnight ~ shown as "turn"
resource time: 4 ~ refill each turn ~ shown as "time left this turn"

character attendant: "the cloakroom attendant" ~ selectable ~ custom ~ pronouns chosen
~ state leaving_early: no

place cloakroom: "the cloakroom"
place lobby: "the lobby"
place ballroom: "the ballroom"
place bar: "the bar"
place office: "the assistant manager’s office"
way cloak_hatch: cloakroom - lobby
way ballroom_doors: lobby - ballroom
way bar_arch: lobby - bar
way office_door: lobby - office

act walk: cost 1 ~ steps 1
act observe: cost 2 ~ watches here ~ quiet
act ask: cost 1 ~ "a question, asked as if it didn’t matter"
act search: cost 2 ~ loud
act plant: cost 1 ~ "a story, told to someone who will pass it on"

archetype cover ~ pronouns they

npc keller: "Anton Keller" ~ pronouns he ~ moves walk ~ suspect ~ in office
~ aka "WREN", "Mr. Lark" ~ pick first
npc vera: "Vera Duclos" ~ pronouns she ~ moves walk ~ suspect ~ in ballroom
npc orme: "Felix Orme" ~ pronouns he ~ moves walk ~ suspect ~ in bar
npc inspector: "Inspector Brandauer" ~ pronouns he ~ moves none ~ in bar
npc bruno: "Bruno, the doorman" ~ like informant ~ pronouns he ~ moves none ~ in lobby
npc lotte: "Lotte, with the cigarette tray" ~ like informant ~ pronouns she ~ moves walk ~ in ballroom

npc wren: "WREN" ~ like cover
npc lark: "Mr. Lark" ~ like cover
npc organist: "the Organist" ~ like cover ~ redacted until telegram.dry

list covers: "the three names" ~ holds wren, lark, organist

item telegram: "a telegram for Mr. Lark, wet through" ~ evidence ~ in cloakroom
~ state by_stove: no
~ state dry: no
item stove: "the cloakroom stove" ~ fixed ~ in cloakroom
item register: "the hotel register" ~ evidence ~ in lobby ~ fixed
item rota: "the staff rota, signed by Keller" ~ evidence ~ in office ~ fixed
item orme_coat: "a tweed overcoat, ticket 31" ~ coat ~ in cloakroom
item vera_coat: "a fox fur, ticket 47" ~ coat ~ in cloakroom
item press_card: "a press card: F. Orme, *Manchester Guardian*" ~ in cloakroom ~ hidden until orme_coat.searched
item score: "four bars of an organ voluntary, with numbers pencilled under the notes" ~ evidence ~ in cloakroom ~ hidden until vera_coat.searched

state searched: no ~ belongs to coat
state named: nobody ~ of suspect
state proofs_given: 0

objective names: "Put a person to each of the three names"
~ done when count(cover, where: some P. {{ it is P }} in notebook) == 3

(((
A death is the hour's ending, not the evening's: the checkpoint takes you
back to the start of the hour. Your notebook comes with you.
)))
checkpoint hour ~ on death ~ shows found ~ each hour

on hour begins nine
~ then set telegram.dry: yes when telegram.by_stove

knowledge world ~ truth
knowledge knows ~ per character ~ learned
knowledge notebook ~ per linker ~ manual ~ reads knows
knowledge dossier ~ for keller ~ learned ~ track
~ starts with {{ wren is keller }}, {{ lark is keller }}

fact names_are: "Three names, two people." ~ means {{ wren is keller }}, {{ lark is keller }}, {{ organist is vera }}

fact telegram_text: "The telegram, dried: WREN TO CONFIRM BY ORGANIST AT MIDNIGHT. ROOM 9 AT TEN." ~ clue ~ means {{ wren met organist }}, {{ lark at room_nine @ new_years_eve.ten }}
fact rota_hand: "Keller signs the staff rota at the foot of every column: *A. Keller*, with an A whose bar doesn’t reach the right-hand stroke." ~ clue
fact orme_bar: "Orme has been at the bar since nine, talking to everyone. Lotte says so, and so does the barman." ~ clue ~ means {{ orme at bar @ new_years_eve.ten }}
fact keller_out: "Bruno: Herr Keller went up the back stairs at ten, and was gone the best part of an hour." ~ clue ~ means {{ keller at room_nine @ new_years_eve.ten }}
fact press: "Orme’s press card: the *Manchester Guardian*, real enough." ~ clue ~ clears
fact lark_hand: "The register says *A. Lark, Zürich*, room 9. The A is Keller’s: the same A that signs the staff rota, with the bar that doesn’t reach the right-hand stroke." ~ proof_who ~ clue ~ means {{ lark is keller }}
fact score_code: "The numbers under Vera’s organ voluntary are a time and a room: 2400, 9." ~ proof_who ~ clue ~ means {{ organist is vera }}, {{ organist met lark }}

:: notebook_rules [rules]
(((
Your notebook's rules and limits. It reads what you know; it holds what
you write. `refuse` stops a note; `flag` lets it stand and circles both,
because the other note might be the wrong one.
)))
rule wears: {{ N is P }} and {{ N at A @ W }} => {{ P at A @ W }} ~ known
rule held: {{ N is P }} in notebook and {{ N is P }} => {{ N held }} ~ in world
never {{ N is A }} and {{ N is B }} and A != B ~ in notebook ~ on contradiction refuse
~ "A name is worn by one person."
never {{ P at A @ W }} and {{ P at B @ W }} and A != B ~ in notebook ~ on contradiction flag
~ "Nobody is in two places in one hour."
never {{ N is P }} and {{ M is P }} and {{ N met M }} ~ in notebook ~ on contradiction flag
~ "Nobody meets themself."

:: dossier_rules [rules]
(((
His rules, in the order he finds you.
)))
rule curious: {{ P searched coat }} => {{ P curious }} ~ in dossier
rule curious_ask: {{ P asked_about N }} and {{ N is keller }} => {{ P curious }} ~ in dossier
rule hunting: {{ P curious }} and {{ P seen_at office }} => {{ P hunting }} ~ in dossier
rule must_go: {{ P hunting }} and {{ P named keller }} => {{ P must_go }} ~ in dossier
rule away: {{ P leaving @ W }} => {{ P gone @ W }} ~ in dossier

:: informant [archetype]
(((
Bruno and Lotte tell Keller everything. `where:` picks whom they notice:
anyone there (`person` is built in: a character or an NPC) who is not the
informant.
)))
--
reaction report
~ when count(person, in: here, where: it != self) >= 1
~ then for each P in all(person, in: here, where: it != self): assert {{ P seen_at here }} in dossier

reaction overhear
~ when you.did(ask) and you.in(here)
~ then assert {{ you asked_about ^topic }} in dossier

reaction gossip
~ when you.did(plant) and you.in(here)
~ then assert story in dossier

:: keller [npc]
--
starts: office

goal office
~ toward office
~ weight 2
(((Room 9 is up the back stairs from his office; at ten he is up there.)))

goal greet_guests
~ toward lobby
~ weight 3
~ when clock.hour in [eight, midnight]

goal read_your_notebook
~ toward cloakroom
~ weight 6
~ when {{ you hunting }} in dossier and not you.in(cloakroom)
~ then assert {{ you named keller }} in dossier when {{ ? is keller }} in notebook

goal the_lights
~ toward cloakroom
~ weight 8
~ when {{ you must_go }} in dossier and clock.hour == eleven and not {{ you gone @ new_years_eve.eleven }} in dossier
~ then play cloakroom:dark when you.in(cloakroom)

reaction notice
~ when you.in(here) and here.is(office)
~ then assert {{ you seen_at office }} in dossier

reaction greet
~ when you.in(here)
~ then play keller:greet
~ once per hour

:: keller:greet
[if {{ you must_go }} in dossier]
@keller (smiling) You look tired. Go home before midnight, I’ll mind the coats myself. I insist.

[if {{ you hunting }} in dossier and not {{ you must_go }} in dossier]
@keller You were in my office. Looking for me, I hope?

[if {{ you curious }} in dossier and not {{ you hunting }} in dossier]
@keller Lotte says you’ve been going through the guests’ pockets. A joke, surely. The Bellevue does not go through pockets.

[if not {{ you curious }} in dossier]
@keller A good crowd. Keep the tickets straight tonight and there’s a bottle in it for you.

:: vera [npc]
--
starts: ballroom

goal sing
~ toward ballroom
~ weight 1

goal smoke
~ toward lobby
~ weight 2
~ when clock.hour == nine

:: orme [npc]
--
starts: bar

goal drink
~ toward bar
~ weight 1

:: lotte [npc]
--
starts: ballroom

goal cigarettes
~ toward cloakroom
~ weight 3
~ when clock.hour in [nine, eleven]

goal cigarettes_bar
~ toward bar
~ weight 2

:: eight [prologue]
At eight o’clock the Bellevue opens its doors to the New Year, and the snow comes in with the guests.

[after 2s]
You take their coats. Fur, tweed, a cape lined with red silk, a child’s duffel with a teddy bear in the pocket. A hundred coats on a hundred hooks, a hundred brass tickets, and the stove ticking in the corner.

[after 2s]
At a quarter past, the page boy brings you a telegram for a Mr. Lark, who is not on any list, and asks you to hold it until he calls. It has been out in the snow. The ink has run.

[note]
Four hours to midnight; each turn, four quarter-hours to spend. Your notebook will tell you when two of your notes can’t both be true. It won’t tell you which.

[end]
> [[Hang the telegram by the stove->cloakroom]] ~ cost 0 ~ then set telegram.by_stove: yes

:: cloakroom
The cloakroom: a counter, a stove, and coats to the ceiling, smelling of snow and other people’s perfume.

[if clock.hour == nine]
The three names go round in your head as you hang coats:

{list covers ~ rotate 2s}

[end]
> [[Read the telegram->cloakroom:telegram]] ~ cost 1
> [[Write in your notebook->notebook]] ~ cost 0

> ~ search
> [[Go through ticket 31->cloakroom:orme]] ~ when not orme_coat.searched ~ then set orme_coat.searched: yes
> [[Go through ticket 47->cloakroom:vera]] ~ when not vera_coat.searched ~ then set vera_coat.searched: yes

:: cloakroom:telegram [act]
learn telegram_text when telegram.dry
--
[quote letter ~ by "telegram for Mr. Lark, handed in at Zürich"]
WREN TO CONFIRM BY {redacted "ORGANIST" until telegram.dry} AT MIDNIGHT. ROOM 9 AT {redacted "TEN" until telegram.dry}.
[end]

[if not telegram.dry]
Two words have run into blue clouds. Paper dries, by a stove.

:: cloakroom:orme [act]
assert {{ you searched coat }} in dossier when count(informant, in: here) >= 1
learn press
--
In the tweed: a pipe, a train timetable, and a press card.

:: cloakroom:vera [act]
assert {{ you searched coat }} in dossier when count(informant, in: here) >= 1
learn score_code
--
In the fur, folded small: four bars of an organ voluntary, and under the notes, in pencil, numbers that are not fingering.

[quote poster]
**HOTEL BELLEVUE**
*New Year’s Eve*
**At midnight: Mme Vera Duclos at the organ**
[end]

:: cloakroom:dark
(((
Played by Keller's `the_lights`, if his dossier says you must go and you
haven't made him think you've gone.
)))
--
At eleven the lights in the cloakroom go out. Only the stove glows. Somebody comes in through the hatch, and doesn’t ask for a coat.

[end]
> [[Throw the stove door open->cloakroom:stove]] ~ cost 0
> [[Keep still among the coats->cloakroom:still]] ~ cost 0

:: cloakroom:stove [act]
retell: "The attendant threw open the stove, and the man in the cloakroom was Keller."
--
Firelight jumps across the room, and Anton Keller is standing in it with a coat over his arm and a wire between his hands, blinking.

Out in the lobby, Bruno shouts. Keller drops the wire and smiles, and goes out to see what the trouble is.

:: cloakroom:still [act]
kill you
--
You stand very still among the coats. The coats don’t help.

:: notebook
(((
Your notebook outlives a death: it is the Linker's, not the attendant's.
)))
--
{note who: cover, is: suspect ~ in notebook}

[if notebook.contradicted]
Two of your notes can’t both be true:

{contradictions ~ in notebook}

[end]
{known about: covers ~ in notebook}

> [[Close it->cloakroom]] ~ cost 0

:: lobby
The lobby: palms, brass, a revolving door that lets in a gust of snow every time it turns. Bruno stands by it in a greatcoat with frogging.

[end]
> [[Read the register->lobby:register]] ~ cost 1 ~ when you.knows.rota_hand
> [[Ask Bruno where Keller went at ten->lobby:bruno]] ~ ask ~ with {topic: wren} ~ when clock.hour >= ten
> [[Tell Bruno you’re leaving before midnight->lobby:leaving]] ~ plant ~ with {story: {{ you leaving @ new_years_eve.eleven }}} ~ then set you.leaving_early: yes

:: lobby:register [act]
learn lark_hand
--
Room 9: *A. Lark, Zürich.* You know that A. You have seen it all evening on the rota, at the bottom of every column.

:: lobby:bruno [act]
learn keller_out
--
@bruno Herr Keller? Up the back stairs at ten. Gone the best part of an hour. I thought he’d gone to be sick. It’s that kind of night.

:: lobby:leaving [act]
--
You tell Bruno your mother is ill. You will be gone before midnight. Bruno is very sorry. Bruno will tell Herr Keller before you have finished your sentence.

:: office
Keller’s office: a desk, a safe, the staff rota pinned to a board, and a door to the back stairs.

[end]
> [[Read the rota->office]] ~ cost 1 ~ when not you.knows.rota_hand ~ then learn rota_hand

:: ballroom
The ballroom: a band of six, two hundred people, and at the far end, the hotel’s small white organ, shut.

[end]
> [[Watch Vera between songs->ballroom:watch]] ~ observe ~ when here.has(vera)

:: ballroom:watch [act]
--
Between songs Vera stands at the organ, not playing it. She opens the lid, looks at the keys, and shuts it again. At the bar, Orme is telling a story with his hands.

:: bar
The bar: noise, mirrors, and the Inspector from the canton in his good suit, off duty and not enjoying it.

[end]
> [[Ask Orme about his evening->bar:orme]] ~ ask ~ with {topic: orme} ~ when here.has(orme)

> ~ when clock.hour >= eleven and named == nobody
> [[Tell the Inspector: {target} is WREN->bar:name]] ~ at suspect ~ cost 2

:: bar:orme [act]
learn orme_bar
--
@orme Here since nine, darling. Ask anyone. I’m writing about the rich at play. They don’t, much.

:: bar:name [act]
set named: target
set proofs_given: count(fact, where: it.is(proof_who) and you.knows(it))
set wren.pronouns: target.pronouns when proofs_given >= 2 and target.is(keller)
--
The Inspector listens with his eyes shut.

[if proofs_given >= 2]
He opens them, puts down his glass, and goes to stand by the organ.

[else]
@inspector A name. Bring me a reason.

:: midnight [finale]
finale when: clock.hour == midnight
--
At midnight the band stops, and in the hush Vera Duclos sits down at the little white organ.

[if named == keller and proofs_given >= 2]
She plays four bars. The Inspector is standing beside her before the fifth. On the back stairs, two constables meet Anton Keller coming down, who was also {all keller.aka}.

[if named != keller and named != nobody]
They take {named} out through the kitchens. Keller holds the door for them, and wishes everyone a happy New Year.

[if named == nobody or (named == keller and proofs_given < 2)]
She plays four bars, and somewhere upstairs a window opens and shuts. In the morning room 9 is empty, and Herr Keller has given notice.

[end]
> [[His notes on you->his_notes]] ~ cost 0

:: his_notes [epilogue]
--
In January the police find a pocket diary in Keller’s office safe. One page is about you.

[quote letter ~ by "A. K."]
{known about: you ~ in dossier ~ with times}
[end]

Of your {count({{ ? is ? }} in notebook)} {plural(count({{ ? is ? }} in notebook), "note")} on the three names, {count({{ ? held }})} {if count({{ ? held }}) == 1 then "was" else "were"} true.

[if not {{ you curious }} in dossier]
{capital(possessive(wren))} only note on you says: *the attendant. Harmless.*

:: found [death]
--
They find you in the morning among the coats, and the hotel says it was the stove: the fumes, in a shut room.

[note]
Back to the start of the hour. You remember what you wrote down. You don’t remember how you knew it.

:: a_wet_telegram_dries [test]
start: eight
do: "Hang the telegram by the stove"
given: wait until new_years_eve.nine
do: "Read the telegram"
expect: you.knows.telegram_text
expect: {{ lark at room_nine @ new_years_eve.ten }} in knows

:: searching_is_seen [test]
start: cloakroom
given: move lotte to cloakroom
do: "Go through ticket 47"
expect: {{ you curious }} in dossier
expect events: nib_shown

:: an_alibi_flags_a_note [test]
start: cloakroom
given: learn orme_bar
given: learn telegram_text
given: note {{ lark is orme }} in notebook
expect: notebook.contradicted ~ ((Orme was at the bar at ten; Lark was in room 9))

:: a_name_is_one_person [test]
start: cloakroom
given: note {{ wren is keller }} in notebook
given: note {{ wren is orme }} in notebook
expect: not {{ wren is orme }} in notebook ~ ((refused))

:: a_planted_story_keeps_him_away [test]
start: lobby
given: assert {{ you must_go }} in dossier
do: "Tell Bruno you’re leaving before midnight"
given: wait until new_years_eve.eleven
expect events: not died

:: dying_keeps_the_notebook [test]
start: cloakroom
given: note {{ lark is keller }} in notebook
given: assert {{ you must_go }} in dossier
given: wait until new_years_eve.eleven
do: "Keep still among the coats"
expect events: died, checkpoint_reached
expect: {{ lark is keller }} in notebook
